# Spatial bath-flux investigation and conditional combined qualification

The approved 15-page Rev3 review PDF and both sealed editions remain unchanged.
This additive study preserves all previous failed raw bath gates and the original
5% cold/1% bath limits. No enclosure, gas, radiation, physical link activation,
new material or carrier-transport model is introduced. The source-referenced
housing plus independent cooler remains a synthetic, unverified assembly.

The first phase is an archived-field audit, not a new PDE solve. Fixed geometric
partitions are registered in data/bath_spatial/diagnostic_plan.json before spatial
results: radial/quadrant/angular bins, nine source-positioned glass annuli,
mounting-hole bands, actual outer contour, ear lobes, hot footprint and projected
hot-route boxes. Local continuum bath flux is unknown. Signed/absolute powers,
field changes and exact discrete residual attribution cannot be relabeled as an
independent local physical error or a qualified recovered flux.

The audit independently reconstructs affine gradients by cross products, actual
one-sided normals/materials, normal heights, transverse sampling offsets and
bath-node temperature variation. A full bath-node test-function identity checks
raw bath flux against weighted internal jumps, other exposed surfaces and the
passive electrical work term. Its reaction comparison is diagnostic only.

Next: independently manufactured 3D mixed-boundary conduction benchmark, then a
preregistered bounded transverse/volume mesh pair if supported by the audit.
A real combined 88-leg case is conditional on an independently passing bath
track. Release further requires a systematically refined combined comparator,
all original current/heat/nonlinear gates and quantified temperature/voltage
sensitivity. No combined case or release is claimed at this initial checkpoint.

## Early archived-field findings

All four native fields map bijectively to their actual meshes and reproduce the
archived raw bath powers. Bath area is333.91981702842mm2, all actual outward
normals are -z and every selected face has one Kovar owner. Glass and pin
undersides are not bath triangles; their adiabatic treatment is a test boundary
condition, not a verified OEM environmental boundary.

For the latest821458-tet field, raw outward power is56.567973mW versus known
input57.193021mW. Independent signed contributions are+59.276068mW and
-2.708095mW; the absolute integral is61.984164mW, with8.738% cancellation.
The exact passive bath-node residual identity closes to7e-18W. Its deficit
is617.301microW weighted internal jumps plus7.747microW weighted other
exterior raw flux; passive electrical work is9.1e-18W. About98.8% of the net
discrepancy is the internal-jump term. This is a diagnostic identity, not a
conservative replacement for the failed raw integral or local continuum truth.

Weighted jumps have opposing broad contributions: approximately+1008microW
in remaining Kovar and-466microW in the hot footprint, with contributions in
all nine seal neighborhoods. Absolute internal weighted jumps total49.033mW;
the largest single support face is0.524% of that absolute total. The most
concentrated1% of faces accounts for64.6%, but no error-quantile mask is used
for refinement and no unique localized physical source is inferred.

Median tangential bath-face maximum edge stays413.942micrometers across both
normal refinements. Owner normal-height medians halve295.961->147.981->73.990
micrometers while transverse apex-offset/height medians grow0.602->1.203->2.940.
Thus normal halving does not yield geometrically similar or transversely
converged boundary samples. From the last matched-face comparison, positive
raw power changes-70.116microW and negative contribution changes+56.261microW;
net power worsens13.855microW. This is an actual solved-field change, not a
known local physical error.

Figures from actual archived triangles and fixed masks are retained under
fem/results/bath_spatial_diagnosis_20261030/figures (signed_raw_bath,
owner_sampling and matched_face_change), together with signed face arrays.
The approved15-page PDF is unchanged.

## Independent manufactured benchmark

Five actual3D HeatSolver cases use an independently meshed source-arc two-ear
Kovar-like extrusion with two mounting holes and nine bores. The exact field is
T=300+z(10+2000x-1500y)-200z^2, k=17.3W/m/K, source6920W/m3; bottom
Dirichlet300K, exact top incoming Neumann flux and analytic side Dirichlet values.
Analytical source/top/bath powers balance to roundoff. This is an operator
benchmark with different side boundary conditions from the package. Its exact
reference integrates each actual polygonal footprint; geometry/model error is
separate from the raw derivative error. It is not OEM or device qualification.

The affine field reproduces the bath flux to3.8e-12relative. Full-refinement
errors are-1.427310%, -0.441175%, -0.375721%; the coarse failure remains
FAILED against the original1% target. The finest free residual is1.68e-10W.
A coarse-transverse/normal-only case gives-0.326463%, also passing. Therefore
the benchmark validates the raw operator and a controlled manufactured
problem; it does NOT prove transverse refinement universally improves device
flux or establish whole-device GCI. The real package must decide that outcome.

Initial body-numbering setup failure and a finest-mesh300000-tet preflight
rejection are retained. An explicit pre-solver resource amendment permits the
323352-tet/63036-node scalar case under350000tets/100000nodes/300s. No
geometry, equation, load or1% target changed.

## Geometry candidates, before new coupled results

A fixed all-bath full owner-star subdivision gives784696tets/192714nodes,
minimumSICN0.0423065. A second full owner-star refinement inside the source
8.75mm central-header circle gives1099293tets/268650nodes, minSICN0.0183512.
The mask is registered before either new coupled field, not fitted to new
errors. Both change only Kovar and glass. Every cold, TEC, pin and other cell
is byte-identical; material volumes and physical contact/exterior areas are
preserved to roundoff. Both actual mesh and Elmer mapping audits pass.

These meshes and registered producers/resource bounds are archived as
GEOMETRY-VERIFIED ONLY in this checkpoint. Coupled runs have independent
actual675496-tet initial fields and3000s/4CPU/12GiB bounds. Their running or
projected values are not final evidence in this diagnosis archive. A later
checkpoint must archive genuine completed fields and original raw gate results.

The boundary audit confirms all bath nodes300K within5.7e-14K and only thermal
Dirichlet tag101. Actual external z=0 areas are333.919817mm2 Kovar and
7.812665mm2 glass; no pin external z=0 bath area. Excluding glass from the bath
is the specified test boundary, not a newly validated OEM sink model.
